// bubbler profile: vesktop
//
// Sound is `pulseaudio`: Vesktop is Electron, whose audio backend opens
// libpulse.so.0 (the string is in /usr/lib/electron40/electron), and the
// socket that grant binds is the one it looks for, for the microphone in
// a call as well as for playback. `pipewire` binds only pipewire-0, the
// native socket, which Electron uses for screen capture rather than for
// sound.
//
// Extra Electron flags go in the private home's vesktop-flags.conf,
// which /usr/bin/vesktop reads from $XDG_CONFIG_HOME. That wrapper also
// sets ELECTRON_OZONE_PLATFORM_HINT itself, so no `env` node here does.
//
// `wayland` is the display, and the only one: the sandbox has no X
// display at all, so the hint above resolves to the socket that grant
// binds.
//
// `dri` is the GPU. Without it Electron composites in software and
// decodes video the same way, which is what a call costs most. Bare, so
// the sandbox gets the render nodes and not the card nodes: no EDID, no
// framebuffer geometry, no other client's buffers.
//
// `network` is the sandbox's own network namespace, which is all this
// needs: everything it talks to is Discord's, and nothing of the host's
// loopback is reachable from it.
//
// Bare by design. Add:
//   dbus
//   portals {
//       screencast
//   }
//     — the file chooser for sending a file, and the source picker for
//       screen sharing. `screencast` is what the picker needs; without
//       the child the bundle grants the chooser and nothing else.
//   pipewire
//     — screen and window sharing in a call: the portal picks the source
//       and hands the stream over PipeWire, so both grants are needed.
//   home-share "Downloads" mode=rw
//     — where an attachment is dragged out to or saved into. Sending a
//       file is the portal file chooser's job, so Pictures and Videos
//       need no share of their own.
//   notify
//     — message notifications. Needs `dbus`.
//   tray
//     — the tray icon, and with it "close to tray". Needs `dbus`.
wayland
dri
pulseaudio
network
command "vesktop"
